references are normal halves, so the tolerance is one ulp at half precision: true
fractional and dynamic half powers are within one ulp at half precision of the f64 reference: true
half powers are f32 powf rounded to half once: true
half powers never call the binary-misused hexp2: true
fractional and dynamic exponents bypass the integer-power helper: true
half powers widen both operands into powf: true
Metal half powers widen both operands into pow: true
a vectorized loop's half powers are f32 pow rounded to half once: true
the vectorized loop's geometry packs on Metal (its f32 Mul twin renders packed): true
every pow call in a vectorized half loop on Metal is the widened scalar form, never a pack or vector operand: true
negative bases under fractional exponents are NaN: true
